{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRange","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRange","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalSimpleSpectrum","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.DiagonalSeparation"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.single_mem_range_of_entry_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.single_mem_range_of_entry_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalRange.lean#L69-L92","doc":"**A nonzero matrix entry promotes to an off-diagonal matrix unit.**  If some element of the\nimage has a nonzero `(T', T)` entry, then `single T' T 1` is itself in the image: sandwich between\nthe two diagonal units and divide by the entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.single_self_mem_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.single_self_mem_range","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalRange.lean#L53-L67","doc":"**Every diagonal matrix unit lies in the image of the seminormal representation.**\n\nThe `q`-Jucys–Murphy images are diagonal *and* separating, which is exactly the hypothesis pair of\n`single_self_mem_of_separating`; the interpolation there does the rest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.diagonal_seminormalRep_qJM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.diagonal_seminormalRep_qJM","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalRange.lean#L40-L51","doc":"`ρ(L_k)` equals the diagonal matrix read off its own diagonal — the form\n`DiagonalSeparation` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}